WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.072
- We are back with Tim Allen, everybody!

00:00:03.072 --> 00:00:04.484
(crowd cheering)

00:00:04.484 --> 00:00:06.870
That was a look at his
new show on Disney Plus,

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.610
it's called the Santa Clauses.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:11.640
And we are also joined by
his very talented co-star

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.400
and real life daughter
now, Elizabeth Allen Dick.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.864
Y'all give it up for her.

00:00:15.864 --> 00:00:17.580
(crowd cheers)

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:18.570
You did so great!

00:00:18.570 --> 00:00:21.060
And I was telling you in the
commercial, but I had no idea,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.490
I didn't put it together
that you were his daughter,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.410
until literally reading
the script for the show.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:27.060
And I was like, "No way!"

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.490
I was like, anyway, You
did such a great job.

00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:32.100
Was it intimidating or
weird to work with your dad?

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.510
- Um, not really, honestly.

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:34.920
It was a blast.

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:38.580
Like, I had so much fun
on set and off screen.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.290
Like, we would finish
a scene he would just

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:41.700
immediately crack a joke about the scene,

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:42.660
and we would just start laughing.

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.220
But it was just a blast.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.470
It was so much fun.

00:00:45.470 --> 00:00:46.740
- I, I love this.

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.630
It's such a cool experience
to have like with your kid,

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.190
like enjoying something
that you love doing.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:51.630
Was it weird for you?

00:00:51.630 --> 00:00:53.490
- Well, I, I, I always set it up,

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:54.920
Her mom and I...

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:58.710
we're neutral about her
being in this business.

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.120
She's really good at school.

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.590
She's really good in athletics at school,

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:04.410
She's really good at math, and
she's a really good student.

00:01:04.410 --> 00:01:05.243
- Yeah.

00:01:05.243 --> 00:01:07.770
- And then for when the Santa
Claus, we decided to do this,

00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.460
there's a lot of elves in it
and I wanted to make her an elf

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.660
as a joke, not a joke,

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:14.460
but if, Happy Christmas,
you're gonna go on set,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.230
and just put on the
ears and wave at Santa.

00:01:16.230 --> 00:01:17.631
So we'll have, have as a memory.

00:01:17.631 --> 00:01:18.464
- Yeah.

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:19.297
- You know, and I,

00:01:19.297 --> 00:01:20.130
- Great memory.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:20.963
- thought about my older
daughter putting in there,

00:01:20.963 --> 00:01:22.980
but elves at 32 years
old seems a little odd.

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:24.557
So, we just...

00:01:24.557 --> 00:01:25.390
- Would've been funny.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:26.223
And we put her in there and she said,

00:01:26.223 --> 00:01:27.180
they said, uh,

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:28.740
if she says hi, she has to read.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:29.670
We gotta get her voice done.

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.340
I said, I, I'm the executive
producer and I'm saying I don't

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.050
want to, nepotist on the side...

00:01:34.050 --> 00:01:35.370
I don't want to push that.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:36.324
- Yeah.

00:01:36.324 --> 00:01:37.157
- And they go, "No, just have her read it.

00:01:37.157 --> 00:01:38.370
We'll just read the
little part we got here."

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:40.260
She read it and the whole
room got real quiet.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.520
And I went, "Wow."

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:44.130
And I heard everybody go, "Hmm,
has she done this before?"

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:47.400
And I go, "No, but I listen,
let's read all the other girls.

00:01:47.400 --> 00:01:48.594
Let's just move on. Move on."

00:01:48.594 --> 00:01:49.427
- Yeah.

00:01:49.427 --> 00:01:51.810
- And she kept reading up the food chain,

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.030
and at one of the best
moments was she read it

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.190
against the studio and all
the big casting people,

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.140
the whole, the whole
place got really quiet.

00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.670
It was on a Zoom audition.

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:00.729
- Yeah.

00:02:00.729 --> 00:02:02.940
- And all the boxes literally
were looking at my box.

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.533
And I, I go, "Uhhhh."

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:08.460
And I was doing a fist pump
'cause she got the joke.

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:12.210
It was a really subtle
joke with her Mrs. Clause.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.043
- Yeah.

00:02:13.043 --> 00:02:15.510
And on the way through it, I
was on the road and she called,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:17.587
they called her and her
mom at the home and said,

00:02:17.587 --> 00:02:18.930
"We'd like her to be the lead."

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:23.460
I said, "I have no way to
describe how, had, she earned it.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:26.160
She did it and she showed
great respect for the crew

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.840
and the staff and she just drilled it."

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:28.976
So...

00:02:28.976 --> 00:02:30.638
- That's awesome.

00:02:30.638 --> 00:02:31.667
I love that story.

00:02:31.667 --> 00:02:33.210
'Cause a lot of people would think

00:02:33.210 --> 00:02:34.043
that you just put her in there,

00:02:34.043 --> 00:02:35.160
but she worked her way
up doing the reading.

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:35.993
- [Tim] Worked her way up and did it.

00:02:35.993 --> 00:02:37.320
- And I love that you were
like, she got the joke.

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:39.960
I'm like, obviously you're her dad.

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:41.970
How does she not get jokes at this point?

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.620
Like, that would be weird.

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.390
But what's the, what's the
show about for everybody?

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.670
My, I was telling him,
me and my kids, we loved,

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.080
we saw two episodes so far.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:50.070
It's so great.

00:02:50.070 --> 00:02:51.390
We love the movies as well.

00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.190
So, it was so great to see it as a series.

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:54.900
Like, what is it about, who do you play?

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:57.210
- So, I play Sandra
Claus, Santa's daughter.

00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:00.150
And I feel like it's,
it starts to dive deep

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.020
into the family and Santa's
family and how his job can get

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:07.830
in the way of family time and
how it really, I mean it does.

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.350
And there's also, people
talk about this more,

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.860
but it answers the questions
that in the old Santa movies,

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.840
that people kind of started asking about

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.060
and that you didn't really ever find out.

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.690
So there's, you know, like
why weren't the elves mad when

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:23.010
just a new Santa arrived?

00:03:23.010 --> 00:03:24.067
- I show up at the North
Pole and they're going,

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.530
"Okay, you gotta get
these package in here."

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.510
And you're thinking,
"Did the other guy die?

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:29.730
Did anybody care about what happened?"

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:31.230
- I loved that part actually.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.063
- Well it's...

00:03:32.063 --> 00:03:33.541
- Because it was weird in the movie!

00:03:33.541 --> 00:03:35.250
The elves were like,
"Well he died, he's done."

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:36.083
Like, yeah.

00:03:36.083 --> 00:03:37.290
- Did, did he die?

00:03:37.290 --> 00:03:38.123
- Yeah. We don't know. I know.

00:03:38.123 --> 00:03:39.540
- We don't know, we'll find out.

00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:42.240
And we go dive deep as it gets later about

00:03:42.240 --> 00:03:44.730
St. Nicholas and the Turkish
priest that started this.

00:03:44.730 --> 00:03:48.690
So it, it honors the heart
of Christmas is about giving.

00:03:48.690 --> 00:03:50.370
It's really important to understand,

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.467
getting is what we've got used to.

00:03:52.467 --> 00:03:53.310
- Receiving. Yeah, yeah.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.143
- Receiving.

00:03:54.143 --> 00:03:57.480
But the whole thing is about
what it's like to give.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:03:59.730
And boy, give is a, a
father to his children

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.030
and give to a giver and
the gift, gift getters.

00:04:03.030 --> 00:04:03.863
- Yeah.

00:04:03.863 --> 00:04:04.890
- It is so magic.

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:06.150
I said I wouldn't have done it.

00:04:06.150 --> 00:04:08.880
Got back in that, that suit just,

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.044
- Oh my God. It has to be.

00:04:10.044 --> 00:04:10.930
- She saw that.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.763
Ugh, I get so angry.

00:04:11.763 --> 00:04:12.596
- So what is that like?

00:04:12.596 --> 00:04:13.429
Walking on set and your dad's Santa?

00:04:13.429 --> 00:04:16.890
- I mean, well the first time
it was, it was really amazing.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:18.660
And I just see him and
he comes around with the

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.930
whole suit on and the,
the full head, the beard,

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.570
the everything and, and
everyone's just kinda like,

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:26.310
up against the walls
like this, and just like,

00:04:26.310 --> 00:04:27.720
looking at him.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:30.000
- Isn't it incredible
what costumes do? Yeah.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:30.833
- It's incredible.

00:04:30.833 --> 00:04:31.666
- Transformative.

00:04:31.666 --> 00:04:32.940
- It's like he's a different person.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.950
But it was, it was really heartwarming

00:04:34.950 --> 00:04:36.390
at the same time, because it's like,

00:04:36.390 --> 00:04:39.810
all of these people saw
him when they were kids,

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.220
you know, in the, in the old movies.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.950
And then now he comes
back on set as Santa.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:44.820
- Yeah.

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:46.050
- As the char, as the
character that he's created.

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:47.580
And it was just, it was insane.

00:04:47.580 --> 00:04:49.806
- It's cool, it's
nostalgic, it's beautiful.

00:04:49.806 --> 00:04:50.639
(crowd clapping)

00:04:50.639 --> 00:04:52.200
And my, and, and kids forever.

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:54.060
That's the cool thing about
doing Christmas stuff,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:57.000
is like, each year, you gain
new fans that are old enough

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.080
to like start watching them.

00:04:58.080 --> 00:04:59.190
Like even my kids are six and eight

00:04:59.190 --> 00:05:00.630
and they've been watching it
for like, a couple years now.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.887
And they, they, 'cause most
of the time they're like,

00:05:02.887 --> 00:05:05.130
"I don't wanna watch a real people movie."

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.660
They're always like, "I
don't want real people."

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.300
But they love, they love
the Santa Claus movie.

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:10.650
So, they were really into watching it

00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:12.700
and it was, it was just really well done.

